# Raster image formats

markdoc-pdf decodes every image from its bytes, so the file extension is only
a hint — a mislabelled file still renders. These are the supported raster
formats; reference any of them with markdown `![](…)` or `\{% media src="…" /%}`
(paths resolve against `--assets-root`, or use an Arca `id`). PNG works
identically, and SVG (vector) appears in the other examples.

## JPEG — good for photographs and gradients

![Blue-to-purple gradient labelled JPEG](sample.jpg)

## GIF — flat colour; animation shows the first frame only

A PDF has no animated raster, so an animated GIF renders its first frame; a
static GIF like this one renders as-is.

![Green tile labelled GIF](sample.gif)

